{"title": "Show HN: Carto – structural intelligence for AI coding agents (OSS)", "link": "https://github.com/theanshsonkar/carto", "summary": "<p>The problem : AI agents fail systematically above 10k LOC. The failure mode are same wrong file, partial completion, tool thrashing, context overflow.<p>Carto fixes this by giving AI agents what they are missing - Domain Map (automatic, no config), blast radius before any change, cross domain violation detection, Agents md for instant codebase context, 16+ mcp tools etc.<p>AI knowing what could break before it start editing  code. Feels like most tools are focus on generating code faster. Maybe the next step is helping AI understand systems better.<p>MIT licensed , Runs entirely local , No data leaks.\nTested on codebase like VScode, prisma, zed and more ( having over 10k+ files)<p>If you have any questions or patterns or ideas lets discuss. There is so much more things that can be done with this coz this thing i made is not just related to programming languages if you u see it u can use it to parse many more types of works.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48380183\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48380183</a></p>\n<p>Points: 1</p>\n<p># Comments: 0</p>", "published": "2026-06-03T05:16:25+00:00", "source": "Hacker News Best", "category": "techblog", "matched_entities": {}, "ontology": {"repo": "BlogRadar", "category": "techblog", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "source_event_model": "blog_post", "event_model_id": "tech.blog_post", "evidence_policy_ids": ["source_metadata", "article_text"], "event_model_payload": {"headline": "Show HN: Carto – structural intelligence for AI coding agents (OSS)", "source_name": "Hacker News Best", "source_url": "https://github.com/theanshsonkar/carto", "published_at": "2026-06-03T05:16:25+00:00", "summary": "<p>The problem : AI agents fail systematically above 10k LOC. The failure mode are same wrong file, partial completion, tool thrashing, context overflow.<p>Carto fixes this by giving AI agents what they are missing - Domain Map (automatic, no config), blast radius before any change, cross domain violation detection, Agents md for instant codebase context, 16+ mcp tools etc.<p>AI knowing what could break before it start editing  code. Feels like most tools are focus on generating code faster. Maybe the next step is helping AI understand systems better.<p>MIT licensed , Runs entirely local , No data leaks.\nTested on codebase like VScode, prisma, zed and more ( having over 10k+ files)<p>If you have any questions or patterns or ideas lets discuss. There is so much more things that can be done with this coz this thing i made is not just related to programming languages if you u see it u can use it to parse many more types of works.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48380183\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48380183</a></p>\n<p>Points: 1</p>\n<p># Comments: 0</p>"}}, "logged_at": "2026-06-03T06:04:22.903237+00:00"}
